{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. Summary:\n\n**Cause** — `similarity()` in `src/app.py` returned a Python float (`round(0.7 * tag + 0.3 * words, 4)`), and boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats (`TypeError: Float types are not supported`). The first publish only succeeded because the table was empty — `similar=0` means an empty list, so no float ever reached DynamoDB. Every later publish computes scores against existing stories and 500s, exactly matching `logs/error.log`.\n\n**Fix** — `similarity()` now computes in `Decimal` end to end and returns a 4-place quantized `Decimal`, which DynamoDB accepts natively, with the same numeric semantics as the old `round(..., 4)`.\n\n**So it can't come back** — added `test_second_publish_with_related_story_succeeds` to `tests/test_publish.py`: it publishes two related stories through the real `handler()` and asserts 201 for both plus `Decimal` scores in the stored item. I confirmed it reproduces the production TypeError before the fix and passes after; both tests are green (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`), and a smoke test with more publishes/re-publishes stored only `Decimal` scores.\n\nFull write-up is in `ANSWER.md`."}
